  "id": "Compound::DB00783 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "Estradiol is implicated in the regulation of Abcb1 through a series of molecular interactions that involve steroid hormones and their metabolites. The evidence suggests that Estradiol directly causes Cervical Discharge, which is linked to Estriol, a metabolite of Estradiol, that binds to Abcb1. Similarly, Estradiol is associated with Abnormal Withdrawal Bleeding, which is linked to Estrone, another metabolite of Estradiol, that also binds to Abcb1. These pathways highlight a consistent mechanism by which Estradiol influences Abcb1 through the action of its metabolites. The presence of multiple independent pathways, each involving Estradiol and a distinct metabolite that binds to Abcb1, suggests that Estradiol may exert its effects on Abcb1 through a network of metabolic interactions. The shared lowest common ancestors—Estradiol and its metabolites—underscore the importance of these pathways in the overall regulation of Abcb1.",
